RustFig is a Rust reimplementation of xfig. Its behaviour follows xfig's
documentation and sources, and parts of it are ported from xfig and fig2dev
(https://mcj.sourceforge.net/). xfig and fig2dev are (c) 1985-1988 Supoj
Sutanthavibul, (c) 1991 Micah Beck, and Brian V. Smith, Paul King, Thomas
Loimer and other contributors, under the xfig licence (SPDX: Xfig), which
permits use, modification, sublicensing and redistribution provided the
copyright and permission notice remain intact. That notice is reproduced
in LICENSE-xfig, which also lists every RustFig file derived from xfig or
fig2dev with its sources; each of those files names its sources in a
comment and points to LICENSE-xfig.

X-splines are implemented from the published paper: C. Blanc and
C. Schlick, "X-Splines: A Spline Model Designed for the End User",
SIGGRAPH '95.

Assets
------
This repository contains no image, icon or font files. Fill patterns and
colour tables are generated in code; the mode panel icons are xfig's
bitmaps from w_icons.c, kept as byte arrays in source code under the xfig
licence (see ASSETS.md and LICENSE-xfig). The attribute pictures are also
drawn as vectors in code (ui-egui/src/vector_icons.rs), RustFig's own work
after xfig's compositions, and xfig's mode icons are traced as vectors
(ui-egui/src/mode_icons.rs). The application icon is an original drawing
generated in code (ui-egui/src/app_icon.rs), MIT OR Apache-2.0.

Fonts used at run time
----------------------
- Optional: fonts from storytold/craft-fonts, embedded only when the build
  sets CRAFT_FONTS_DIR; their licences ship with that repository.
- Fallback: Ubuntu Light (Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0) and Hack (MIT/Bitstream
  Vera licence), bundled inside the `epaint_default_fonts` crate (a
  dependency, MIT OR Apache-2.0), used for canvas and bitmap text.

Third-party Rust crates are used under their own licences (MIT, Apache-2.0,
BSD, Zlib and similar permissive licences); see Cargo.lock.
